# One-time 100% depreciation

`household.oneTimeDepreciation` (optional list of `{ id, label, amount, year }`)
is entered from the plan summary on the left (One-time depreciation, Add),
not from a wizard step. Several entries are allowed, in the same or
different years.

## Engine

In each entry's year `projectScenario` deducts the full amount from federal
taxable income (`deductions.oneTimeDepreciation`, part of
`deductions.total`) and from state taxable income
(`stateDeductions.oneTimeDepreciation`, part of `stateDeductions.total`).
Per entry amounts are on the row as `oneTimeDepreciationById`. Both
scenarios get it.

- Taxable income never goes below 0; an excess is not carried forward (no
  NOL).
- It's a deduction, not lower gross income, so Medicare MAGI (IRMAA) and the
  senior deduction phase-out don't change. Same pattern as rental
  depreciation.
- The lower tax raises that year's surplus, which isn't banked, so assets and
  inheritance don't move.

## UI

- Main: a "100% depreciation" section after Cash flow, one line per asset,
  shown only when a year in the window has some.
- Main in detail analysis: "100% depreciation" under Deductions and State
  deductions, with one child per asset when there are several.

`migrateHousehold` keeps only entries with an id, a year and a positive
amount. Golden case: `one-time-depreciation.json`.
